	quest.0F383CC15654A0F1.quest_subtitle: "a marriage of necessity"
	quest.0F383CC15654A0F1.title: "merging"
	quest.0F3A6DBAE66E8E86.quest_desc: ["Enrich the &85 dirty dusts&r into &e5 clean dusts&r."]
	quest.0F3A6DBAE66E8E86.quest_subtitle: "Clean x5"
	quest.0F3A6DBAE66E8E86.title: "&4&lEnriching&r"
	quest.0F401394EE48EEDF.quest_desc: [
		"&7Head protection with a little something extra.&r"
		""
		"&8Farm your resources. &dMystical Agriculture&7 grows what miners dig.&r"
	]
	quest.0F401394EE48EEDF.quest_subtitle: "Cover your head"
	quest.0F401394EE48EEDF.title: "Inferium Helmet"
	quest.0F57CE5F4144E92B.quest_desc: [
		"Because 8 blocks wasn't far enough. Shoot items up to 24 blocks away."
		""
		"Still not cross-dimensional, but we're getting there."
	]
	quest.0F57CE5F4144E92B.quest_subtitle: "Stronger yeet"
	quest.0F57CE5F4144E92B.title: "&c&lSender Module Mk2&r"
	quest.0F69CC5607B47DDD.quest_desc: ["Smashes things together violently."]
	quest.0F69CC5607B47DDD.quest_subtitle: "Violent hugs"
	quest.0F69CC5607B47DDD.title: "&e&lAbsolute Combining Factory&r"
	quest.0F7395397129061F.quest_desc: ["&7Seven slots. An industrial-scale black hole for cobblestone."]
	quest.0F7395397129061F.quest_subtitle: "&4Black hole"
	quest.0F7395397129061F.title: "&4Elite Recycling Factory"
	quest.0F872CFD479435D5.quest_desc: [
		"The chapter widens out from here."
		""
		"Craft or obtain the &bFlux Controller&r."
		"The brain of the system. Everything else connects back to this block, and it is where you configure the network as a whole."
		"Part of the &7Flux Networks&r progression."
		"&8Take it or leave it - the chapter continues elsewhere."
	]
	quest.0F872CFD479435D5.quest_subtitle: "&7Flux Networks"
	quest.0F872CFD479435D5.title: "&bFlux Controller"
	quest.0F8F593BE05C06E6.quest_desc: ["&bfreezes mobs&7 and not careful players in place. useful to subdue withers for &dether gas harvest&7"]
	quest.0F8F593BE05C06E6.quest_subtitle: "slow down mf"
	quest.0F8F593BE05C06E6.title: "&bpress (c) to use stasis to slow enemies"
	quest.0F912AD6541F2053.quest_desc: [
		"From Runewood, the ancients raised their Totems. Pillars that sang to the unseen. Each was bound with the mark of a spirit, its log attuned through deliberate rite. When a full set of symbols is carved, the totem’s base may be awakened, invoking the Spirit Rite bound within."
		""
		"Every Rite manifests power differently: some warp the world, others bless or curse those who stand nearby. Beware, two of the same Rite, when invoked together, cancel one another out, their voices lost in discord."
		""
		"A &dTotemic Staff&r reveals the totem’s domain, the invisible field in which its influence breathes. Use it to inscribe glow upon attuned logs... for power unlit is merely promise unfulfilled."
	]
	quest.0F912AD6541F2053.quest_subtitle: "Wood carved with purpose becomes more than tree."
	quest.0F912AD6541F2053.title: "&dRunewood Totem&r"
	quest.0F9A8F34ADE240C2.title: "First Steps"
	quest.0FA6B74C8EED7C90.quest_desc: ["&7at least &eone&7 is required for laser bases to work"]
	quest.0FA6B74C8EED7C90.quest_subtitle: "&7Industrial Foregoing"
	quest.0FA6B74C8EED7C90.title: "&bLaser Drill"
	quest.0FAB9E271D252512.quest_desc: [
		"A natural continuation of the previous step."
		""
		"Craft or obtain the &bMycelial Slimey&r."
		"Another piece of the machine chain. On its own it does little; wired into the rest of your factory it removes one more job you were doing by hand."
		"Part of the &7Industrial Foregoing&r progression."
		"&8The end of this branch."
	]
	quest.0FAB9E271D252512.quest_subtitle: "&7Industrial Foregoing"
	quest.0FAB9E271D252512.title: "&bMycelial Slimey"
	quest.0FC85E6638297291.quest_subtitle: "Store your items and display them beautifully."
	quest.0FEDC1FA9EC86E8E.quest_desc: [
		"It &ccrushes&r things."
		""
		"Mostly &abio-matter&r, occasionally your hopes and dreams when you realize you need a dozen of these."
	]
	quest.0FEDC1FA9EC86E8E.quest_subtitle: "Smashy smashy"
	quest.0FEDC1FA9EC86E8E.title: "&7&lCrusher&r"
	quest.0FF57ABA17099636.quest_desc: [
		"&7Oritech machines are fully modular!"
		""
		"&7To upgrade them, you don't put cards inside - you physically place addon blocks next to the machine, creating Multiblock structures. Increase efficiency and production speed."
	]
	quest.0FF57ABA17099636.title: "&aMultiblock Addons"
	quest.0FFD3BF146450892.quest_desc: ["&9Soul-Touched Deepshelves&r are an upgrade to &9Deepshelves&r. \\n\\nThey are Crafted with a &bSoul Lantern&r and 3 &3Sculk Blocks&r. You'll need &5Silk Touch&r to pick up &3Sculk Blocks&r. \\n\\nThen, we can Craft our &9Soul-Touched&r version. These will give a ton more &cQuanta&r at &c15%&r! \\n\\nIt also increases max &aEterna&r to &a75&r."]
	quest.0FFD3BF146450892.title: "&9Soul-Touched Deepshelf"
	quest.1000000000000001.quest_desc: ["Craft a Technologium Ingot in the Extreme Crafting Table."]
	quest.1000000000000001.quest_subtitle: "The pinnacle of technological achievement."
	quest.1000000000000001.title: "Technologium"
	quest.1000000000000002.quest_desc: ["Craft an Adventurite Ingot in the Extreme Crafting Table."]
	quest.1000000000000002.quest_subtitle: "Born from hundreds of expeditions."
	quest.1000000000000002.title: "Adventurite"
	quest.1000000000000003.quest_desc: ["Craft a Magite Ingot in the Extreme Crafting Table."]
	quest.1000000000000003.quest_subtitle: "The pure essence of magic."
	quest.1000000000000003.title: "Magite"
	quest.1000000000000004.quest_desc: ["Combine the power of Technologium, Adventurite, and Magite along with other artifacts to create the Adovtech Heart."]
	quest.1000000000000004.quest_subtitle: "The ultimate goal."
	quest.1000000000000004.title: "Adovtech Heart"
	quest.1000000000000013.quest_desc: [
		"Gold sits comfortably in the middle of the progression: cheap enough to mass-produce, strong enough to matter."
		"The &6Gold Generator&r burns solid fuel far more aggressively than the earlier tiers and delivers a steady supply to a growing machine hall."
		"At this point it is worth wiring your generators into a proper &benergy network&r rather than cabling each machine individually - Powah cells or Flux Networks both work well."
		"Two exotic branches open here: alchemical power from potions, and sweet, sticky throughput from honey."
		"&8Next: Diamond tier, or the Potion and Honey generators."
	]
	quest.1000000000000013.quest_subtitle: "&7The golden mean of solid fuel"
	quest.1000000000000013.title: "&bGold Generator"
	quest.1000000000000014.quest_desc: [
		"&bGold Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000014.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000014.title: "&bGold Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000016.quest_desc: [
		"Brewing has always been a side activity. Here it becomes a power source."
		"The &dPotion Generator&r consumes potions and scales its output with their &5brewing complexity&r - the more steps a potion took to create, the more energy it yields."
		"Splash and lingering variants of heavily-modified potions are the most valuable fuel of all."
		"Automating this is a genuine engineering puzzle, best solved with Create or Super Factory Manager."
		"&8A rewarding detour rather than a mainline power source."
	]
	quest.1000000000000016.quest_subtitle: "&5Alchemical power generation"
	quest.1000000000000016.title: "&dPotion Generator"
	quest.1000000000000017.quest_desc: [
		"&dPotion Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000017.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000017.title: "&dPotion Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000018.quest_desc: [
		"&dPotion Generator (64x)&r"
		""
		"The &a64x variant&r is the compressed form of this generator line - sixty-four units of generation and buffer capacity condensed into one block."
		"Server performance improves noticeably when you replace large generator banks with these, since the game only has to tick a single block entity."
		"Feeding one requires serious fuel infrastructure. Plan the supply chain first, then build the generator."
		"&8The most compact form this generator line can take."
	]
	quest.1000000000000018.quest_subtitle: "&7Sixty-four generators, one block"
	quest.1000000000000018.title: "&dPotion Generator (64x)"
	quest.1000000000000019.quest_desc: [
		"Bees are among the most self-sufficient farms in Minecraft, and honey is the result."
		"The &eHoney Generator&r runs on liquid honey, giving you a completely renewable fluid fuel that needs no mining, no Nether trips and no combat."
		"Set up a bee wall with hives and a Create pump, and this generator will run indefinitely with no further input."
		"Output is modest, but the running cost is effectively zero."
		"&8Ideal for early automated bases that want to stay hands-off."
	]
	quest.1000000000000019.quest_subtitle: "&7Sweet, sticky, renewable energy"
	quest.1000000000000019.title: "&eHoney Generator"
	quest.1000000000000020.quest_desc: [
		"&eHoney Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000020.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000020.title: "&eHoney Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000021.quest_desc: [
		"&eHoney Generator (64x)&r"
		""
		"The &a64x variant&r is the compressed form of this generator line - sixty-four units of generation and buffer capacity condensed into one block."
		"Server performance improves noticeably when you replace large generator banks with these, since the game only has to tick a single block entity."
		"Feeding one requires serious fuel infrastructure. Plan the supply chain first, then build the generator."
		"&8The most compact form this generator line can take."
	]
	quest.1000000000000021.quest_subtitle: "&7Sixty-four generators, one block"
	quest.1000000000000021.title: "&eHoney Generator (64x)"
	quest.1000000000000022.quest_desc: [
		"Diamond-grade generators are the first tier that can realistically keep a mid-game factory fed on its own."
		"The &bDiamond Generator&r combines a large fuel efficiency bonus with a deep energy buffer, smoothing out the spikes that come from batch-processing machines."
		"By now your fuel supply should be automated - a tree farm feeding a charcoal kiln, or Create-powered coal processing."
		"Manual refuelling stops scaling long before this tier does."
		"&8Next: Emerald tier, plus the Ender and Obsidian branches."
	]
	quest.1000000000000022.quest_subtitle: "&7High-end burning for demanding factories"
	quest.1000000000000022.title: "&bDiamond Generator"
	quest.1000000000000023.quest_desc: [
		"&bDiamond Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000023.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000023.title: "&bDiamond Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000025.quest_desc: [
		"Ender Pearls carry a fragment of the End inside them - and that energy can be released."
		"The &5Ender Generator&r burns Ender Pearls and Eyes of Ender for a strong, concentrated power boost with very little fuel volume."
		"Because the fuel stacks so densely, a single hopper feed will keep this running for a very long time between refills."
		"An Enderman farm or an Industrial Foregoing mob crusher will supply far more pearls than you need."
		"&8Excellent for compact, low-maintenance power rooms."
	]
	quest.1000000000000025.quest_subtitle: "&5Void energy, tapped directly"
	quest.1000000000000025.title: "&5Ender Generator"
	quest.1000000000000026.quest_desc: [
		"&5Ender Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000026.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000026.title: "&5Ender Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000027.quest_desc: [
		"&5Ender Generator (64x)&r"
		""
		"The &a64x variant&r is the compressed form of this generator line - sixty-four units of generation and buffer capacity condensed into one block."
		"Server performance improves noticeably when you replace large generator banks with these, since the game only has to tick a single block entity."
		"Feeding one requires serious fuel infrastructure. Plan the supply chain first, then build the generator."
		"&8The most compact form this generator line can take."
	]
	quest.1000000000000027.quest_subtitle: "&7Sixty-four generators, one block"
	quest.1000000000000027.title: "&5Ender Generator (64x)"
	quest.1000000000000028.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have a reliable lava supply, obsidian stops being a chore and becomes a bulk resource."
		"The &8Obsidian Generator&r trades a little raw output for exceptional durability and a very large internal buffer, making it ideal for remote outposts and mining bases that you do not visit often."
		"It burns the same solid fuels as the metal tiers, so it slots into an existing fuel network with no changes."
		"Pair it with a Mekanism Pump or a Create fluid setup to keep obsidian production running hands-free."
		"&8Next: the Emerald tier awaits."
	]
	quest.1000000000000028.quest_subtitle: "&7Slow to build, impossible to break"
	quest.1000000000000028.title: "&bObsidian Generator"
	quest.1000000000000029.quest_desc: [
		"&bObsidian Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000029.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000029.title: "&bObsidian Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000031.quest_desc: [
		"Emerald generators represent the practical limit of what conventional combustion can achieve."
		"The &aEmerald Generator&r pushes enormous amounts of Forge Energy per tick and is capable of running an entire Mekanism processing line by itself."
		"Emeralds are best acquired through trade halls or Mystical Agriculture crops rather than mining - plan for a renewable supply before committing to a bank of these."
		"The final two exotic branches unlock here: enchantment recycling and dragon's breath."
		"&8Next: Netherite, and then the true endgame."
	]
	quest.1000000000000031.quest_subtitle: "&7Approaching the ceiling of solid fuel"
	quest.1000000000000031.title: "&bEmerald Generator"
	quest.1000000000000032.quest_desc: [
		"&bEmerald Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
	]
	quest.1000000000000032.quest_subtitle: "&7Eight generators in a single block"
	quest.1000000000000032.title: "&bEmerald Generator (8x)"
	quest.1000000000000034.quest_desc: [
		"Enchanting produces a great deal of waste: badly-rolled books, junk loot gear, unwanted rolls from Apotheosis."
		"The &dEnchantment Generator&r strips enchantments off items and converts the magic directly into Forge Energy, scaling with the level and rarity of what it consumes."
		"This closes a satisfying loop - energy powers your enchanting setup, and the failures feed back into the energy supply."
		"Combine it with an automated Apothic Enchanting table for a self-sustaining cycle."
		"&8A superb sink for dungeon loot you would otherwise throw away."
	]
	quest.1000000000000034.quest_subtitle: "&5Recycle magic into machinery"
	quest.1000000000000034.title: "&dEnchantment Generator"
	quest.1000000000000035.quest_desc: [
		"&dEnchantment Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
		"This is the correct answer to a power room that has outgrown its floor space."
		"Fuel consumption scales with output, so make sure your supply line can keep up before you replace a bank of standard generators."
		"&8Crafted from eight of the previous tier."
