		""
		"The &a64x variant&r is the compressed form of this generator line - sixty-four units of generation and buffer capacity condensed into one block."
		"Server performance improves noticeably when you replace large generator banks with these, since the game only has to tick a single block entity."
		"Feeding one requires serious fuel infrastructure. Plan the supply chain first, then build the generator."
		"&8The most compact form this generator line can take."
	]
	quest.1000000000000036.quest_subtitle: "&7Sixty-four generators, one block"
	quest.1000000000000036.title: "&dEnchantment Generator (64x)"
	quest.1000000000000037.quest_desc: [
		"Few fuels are as thematically satisfying as the breath of the Ender Dragon."
		"The &5Halitosis Generator&r consumes Dragon's Breath to produce a respectable and highly compact stream of energy."
		"Dragon's Breath is renewable - the dragon can be resummoned indefinitely - but collecting it at scale requires either automation or a great deal of patience."
		"Treat this as a prestige generator: interesting, characterful, and a fine excuse to build a dragon farm."
		"&8The 64x variant is genuinely competitive with the metal tiers."
	]
	quest.1000000000000037.quest_subtitle: "&5Dragon's breath, bottled and burned"
	quest.1000000000000037.title: "&5Halitosis Generator"
	quest.1000000000000038.quest_desc: [
		"&5Halitosis Generator (8x)&r"
		""
		"The &a8x variant&r does exactly what the name suggests: eight times the generation rate and eight times the internal buffer, in the footprint of a single block."
